<title>FRANCE: Algeria's cellulose firm loses 800 million dinars.</title>
<headline>Algeria's cellulose firm loses 800 million dinars.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's only cellulose company, Entreprise Nationale de la Cellulose et du Papier (Celpap), made an 800 million dinars ($14.2 million) loss in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>State-owned Celpap, which employs 2,000 workers, had 5.8 billion dinars ($103 million) turnover in 1995, said APS.</p>
<p>The company did not publish results for 1996.</p>
</text>
